Output (what it produces and writes back)
Field	Type	How it's decided
summary	string	one-line LLM-generated summary of the issue
module	enum (8 values)	LLM pick, grounded in the ticket text
category	enum (9 values)	LLM pick
severity	enum (4 values)	deterministic from priority if it maps cleanly; otherwise falls back to the LLM's own read
resolution_type	enum (9 values) or null	only ever set if status is resolved/closed and resolution_notes exist — otherwise forced to "not recorded," never guessed
confidence	0–1	LLM's self-reported confidence
reasoning	string	short justification, checked to actually reference the values it returned (no contradicting itself)
curation_status	AutoApproved or PendingReview	deterministic rule, not the LLM's call: confidence ≥ 0.72 (same threshold backend/taxonomy.py already uses elsewhere) → auto-approved, else sent for human review
